# Docker build context excludes for `docker build -f apps/anytools-web/Dockerfile .`
#
# Keep in mind the build context is the WHOLE repo root (monorepo COPY . . in the
# `builder` stage) — anything needed at build time (packages/**, apps/anytools-web/content,
# LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md) must NOT be excluded here. `public/third-party` is
# excluded on purpose: `apps/anytools-web/package.json`'s `build` script runs
# `copy-vendor-assets.mjs` before `next build`, so it is regenerated inside the image —
# shipping the host's copy in the build context would just be ~54MB of dead weight.

.git
plans
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
packages/anytools-tools/fixtures
apps/anytools-web/public/third-party
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
.claude
workers
.github
